  "resolvedResearchContext": "Retained Wikipedia Russian grammar oldid1369617627, catalog/sources/units-26-30/wikipedia/russian-grammar-1369617627.txt, CC BY-SA 4.0 under retained FREEZE rights attestation: complete Adjectival participle introduction and Active present participle / Active past participle sections. The already admitted living form is the example immediately under Active present participle; the separate reading examples distinguish past and present. This bounded classification identifies participial tense, not the time of an unseen sentence or a productive formation algorithm. Original reversal followed its literal prompt; its defect was awarding time-comprehension credit for choosing the complementary label, not mistranslating a form. Replace it with the distinct already admitted living form. Independently authored English on 2026-10-13 within content-audit-2026-10-08; no new Russian forms, copied primary prose or private Penguin text; qualified semantic audit pending.\nContext explanation:\n\u0436\u0438\u0432\u0443\u0301\u0449\u0438\u0435 means living and is the active present participle in the supplied example: the people perform the living action. Select in the present for this form itself. The past label describes a different participial tense; living gives the lexical meaning rather than the requested time classification. This identifies the admitted form, not the tense of an unseen sentence.\nTuple-v1:tuple-v1:1;16:\u0436\u0438\u0432\u0443\u0301\u0449\u0438\u043514:in the present2;11:in the past6:living",
